                <pb facs="0914" n="826" sameAs="frus:frus1904/pg826"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr.
                            Leishman.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1904-08-10"><hi rendition="#italic">August 10,
                        1904</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Hay states that the character of the visit of the United States fleet must
                    be determined by Mr. Leishman and the Turkish Government, as no communication is
                    possible with it before its arrival at Smyrna. If its presence is no longer
                    required it will be withdrawn immediately upon being notified to that effect by
                    Mr. Leishman.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
